/* ============================================================================
   Cluck Wars — UI Toolkit theme (menu front-end)
   Look: Direction A "Barnyard Toybox" with painted-wood trim (spec
   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-menu-ui-overhaul.md, "Visual system").
   The values below are the tokens in CluckWarsTokens.uss (Direction A block),
   written out literally because this sheet is attached per page template and
   a :root custom property is not guaranteed to reach it:
       ink #2a1a0c   cream #fff8e8 / inset #f3e6c8   gold #f5c842 / edge #d9a521
       CTA green #7be35c -> #36a82c   wood #8a5a2e / #7a4a22
   Three value steps: the backdrop (MenuUiController backdrop, tinted per page),
   wood panels (PanelFrame / CardBg 9-slices), raised cream cards with ink text.
   Button rule: ONE green CTA per screen (the forward action); gold means
   selection / "you" only; wood means navigation and frames.

   Display type (Lilita One: titles, buttons, ribbons) carries a thick ink
   -unity-text-outline plus a hard text-shadow. Both were verified to render on
   Unity 6000.3 in an off-screen capture on 2026-10-06 (the old "no
   text-shadow" ban dated from an older branch). Still NOT available: box-shadow,
   gap, linear-gradient, inherit - depth comes from the baked atoms
   (ButtonGrayscale bevel, GlossOverlay, PanelFrame/CardBg/CardGlowFrame
   9-slices) and rounded corners are border-radius + overflow:hidden.
   Class/ability colors & the chicken sprite are applied in C# at bind time
   (MenuUiController). Fonts are set on the root in C# (UiGfx.ChunkyFont) as a
   guaranteed fallback; url() font refs below are the primary path.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   MOBILE SIZING CONTRACT  (2026-07-23 Android pass) — READ BEFORE EDITING
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Android is the primary target and the app is landscape-locked
   (ProjectSettings: autorotate portrait = 0). Assets/Resources/PanelSettings
   is ScaleWithScreenSize, reference 1920x1080, MatchWidthOrHeight 0.5, so

       scale = sqrt((screenW / 1920) * (screenH / 1080))

   On phones, pixel density rises with resolution, so `scale * 160 / ppi`
   lands in a tight band whatever the handset:

       Pixel 9        2424x1080 @422ppi   scale 1.124   0.426 dp per px
       1344p flagship 2992x1344 @486ppi   scale 1.392   0.458 dp per px
       budget 720p    1600x720  @270ppi   scale 0.745   0.441 dp per px

   => 1 dp ~= 2.35 USS px on this canvas.  Derived floors, which every rule
   below respects:

       touch target   48 dp  ->  116 px   (min-height AND min-width)
       body / button  16 sp  ->   38 px
       readable text  14 sp  ->   34 px   <- hard floor for anything load-bearing
       caption        12 sp  ->   30 px   <- decorative / secondary only

   The pre-2026-07-23 sheet used 9–20 px type and ~40–70 px controls, i.e.
   4–9 sp text and 17–30 dp targets — roughly a third of the Android minimum.
   Consequence of the fix: on a 1920x1080 desktop window the menu renders
   chunky rather than dense. That is deliberate; the phone is the target and
   the arcade art style carries it. Do NOT "fix" it by shrinking type — shrink
   the PanelSettings reference resolution only if you re-derive this table
   AND re-check Assets/UI/Styles/TouchControls.uss, whose HIT TARGETS are
   already phone-correct (150 px hex = 64 dp, joystick base 280 px = 119 dp)
   and would break if the reference moved. (Its *type* was not fine — the hex
   label was 6.4 sp and the slot badge 8.5 sp until the 2026-07-23 sweep.)

   This contract governs every surface, not just this sheet:
     Assets/UI/Styles/MatchTopBar.uss    glanceable HUD, 30-52 px
     Assets/UI/Styles/MatchOverlays.uss  full-screen modals, 34 px floor
     Assets/UI/Styles/TouchControls.uss  targets 150 px, type 28-46 px
     MatchHud.cs      UGUI Canvas — same ScaleWithScreenSize 1920x1080 @0.5
     DebugHud.cs      IMGUI — no scaler exists, so it scales GUI.matrix by dpi
   ============================================================================ */

/* ---- Screen root + pages -------------------------------------------------- */
/* Transparent since stage 2: every page sits on the shared backdrop that
   MenuUiController puts behind all of them (.cw-backdrop below). */
.cw-screen {
    flex-grow: 1;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    overflow: hidden;
    align-items: stretch;
    justify-content: flex-start;
}
.cw-page { flex-grow: 1; align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start; }
.cw-hidden { display: none; }

/* ---- Typography ----------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Headings stay on one line (nowrap) so ribbons/badges grow to fit instead of
   wrapping like the old UGUI ("CHA / RACT"). Body text wraps normally.
   Sizes follow the ramp in the mobile sizing contract above. */
.cw-title, .cw-heading, .cw-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);               /* #fef5e0 */
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Display treatment: thick ink outline + hard drop shadow. Shared by every
   Lilita One element that sits on art or on a coloured face (titles, ribbons,
   buttons, cast names, panel headings). Not used for ink text on cream -
   an ink outline on ink text only thickens it. */
.cw-title, .cw-heading, .cw-label, .cw-btn, .cw-home-btn, .cw-mini-btn,
.cw-menu-cast__name, .cw-pick-row__title, .cw-players-title, .cw-sheet__title {
    -unity-text-outline-width: 4px;
    -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    text-shadow: 0px 5px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85);
}
/* UI Toolkit draws the outline TMP-style, half of it INSIDE the glyph, so a
   width that suits 84 px type would eat 30 px type. Measured on 2026-10-06:
   6 px on titles, 4 px on buttons/headings, 3 px below ~36 px. */
.cw-title { -unity-text-outline-width: 6px; text-shadow: 0px 8px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.9); }
.cw-menu-cast__name, .cw-pick-row__title { -unity-text-outline-width: 3px; text-shadow: 0px 3px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85); }

/* Body text that sits directly on the backdrop art (not on a card): a thin
   ink outline is what keeps it legible over the painted plate. */
.cw-on-art {
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 2px;
    -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    text-shadow: 0px 3px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.8);
}
.cw-title   { font-size: 84px; letter-spacing: 4px; }   /* 36 sp */
.cw-heading { font-size: 48px; letter-spacing: 2px; }   /* 20 sp */
.cw-label   { font-size: 40px; }                        /* 17 sp */

.cw-body {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 34px;                                    /* 14 sp — the floor */
    color: rgb(196, 160, 96);                /* #c4a060 secondary */
    white-space: normal;
}

.cw-accent    { color: rgb(245, 200, 66); }  /* #f5c842 */
.cw-text-dark { color: rgb(26, 14, 4); }

/* ---- Backdrop (one element behind every page) ------------------------------
   MenuUiController.BuildAll puts #Backdrop + #BackdropTint behind the page host
   and swaps image/tint per page (MenuUiController.Backdrops). The image is
   set here as the default so a page without an entry still has the barn. */
.cw-backdrop {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Backgrounds/MenuBackground.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-and-crop;
}
/* "Lift": the plate is a dusk render; a warm wash raises it toward golden hour
   and softens its detail so the cream cards and outlined type read over it.
   Colour/alpha are set per page in C#; this is only the fallback. */
.cw-backdrop-tint {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-color: rgba(255, 196, 120, 0.22);
}
/* Safe-area host: every page lives inside it; MenuUiController.ApplySafeArea
   pads it from Screen.safeArea so nothing lands under a notch or the gesture
   bar while the backdrop still bleeds to the screen edges. */
.cw-page-host { flex-grow: 1; }

/* ---- Value steps: wood panel / cream card / inset --------------------------
   Wood panel = PanelFrame 9-slice (96 px corners at half scale). */
.cw-wood-panel {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/PanelFrame.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 96; -unity-slice-right: 96; -unity-slice-top: 96; -unity-slice-bottom: 96;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.5px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
/* Dark wood well = CardBg 9-slice (the pick rows on the loadout). */
.cw-wood-well {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/CardBg.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 56; -unity-slice-right: 56; -unity-slice-top: 56; -unity-slice-bottom: 56;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.5px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
/* Raised cream card with an ink outline. */
.cw-raised {
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 18px; border-top-right-radius: 18px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 18px; border-bottom-right-radius: 18px;
}
/* Inset well on a cream card. */
.cw-inset {
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35);
    border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
}
/* Selection glow = CardGlowFrame 9-slice as an overlay child that bleeds just
   outside its card. Hidden unless the parent is selected (class chips) or the
   controller adds it (picked ability card, your lobby card). The ring sits at
   52/400 of the source, so at slice-scale 0.6 an inset of -27 puts it ~4 px
   outside the card's ink border. First child, picking ignored. */
.cw-glow {
    position: absolute; left: -27px; top: -27px; right: -27px; bottom: -27px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/CardGlowFrame.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-slice-left: 72; -unity-slice-right: 72; -unity-slice-top: 72; -unity-slice-bottom: 72;
    -unity-slice-scale: 0.6px;
}
.cw-class-chip > .cw-glow { display: none; }
.cw-class-chip.cw-card--selected > .cw-glow { display: flex; }

/* Ink text steps for cream surfaces (contrast on #fff8e8 / #f3e6c8):
   ink ~16:1, soft brown ~7:1 - both clear 4.5:1. */
.cw-ink       { color: rgb(42, 26, 12); }
.cw-ink-soft  { color: rgb(107, 74, 42); }

/* Monochrome glyph font (Noto Emoji) for the few symbols the brand fonts lack:
   the gear and the padlock. Tinted by `color` like any text. */
.cw-glyph {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf");
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* Reduced motion: the root carries .cw-reduced-motion while
   PlayerPreferences.ReducedMotionEnabled is on, which zeroes every hover/press
   scale transition and selection pop in the menus. */
.cw-reduced-motion * { transition-duration: 0s; }
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-btn:hover, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-btn:active,
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-home-btn:hover, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-home-btn:active,
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-ability-card:hover, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-spec-pill:hover,
.cw-reduced-motion .cw-spec-pill:active, .cw-reduced-motion .cw-class-chip:hover { scale: 1 1; }

/* ---- Glossy surfaces ------------------------------------------------------ */
.cw-panel {
    background-color: rgb(58, 34, 16);        /* #3a2210 */
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(138, 106, 58); border-right-color: rgb(138, 106, 58);
    border-top-color: rgb(138, 106, 58); border-bottom-color: rgb(138, 106, 58);
    border-top-left-radius: 22px; border-top-right-radius: 22px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 22px; border-bottom-right-radius: 22px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/GlossOverlay.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
}

.cw-card {
    background-color: rgb(58, 40, 22);        /* #3a2816 */
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-right-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-bottom-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-left-radius: 18px; border-top-right-radius: 18px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 18px; border-bottom-right-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/GlossOverlay.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.cw-card--selected { scale: 1.04 1.04; }

/* ---- Buttons -------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* The Stage-0 ButtonGrayscale atom (9-slice 52) is a beveled glossy pill, tinted
   per-variant at runtime — replaces flat bg-color + Gloss + colored borders.
   No element border (the bevel is baked); tint colours are pushed brighter than
   the target since -unity-background-image-tint-color multiplies the ~grey face.
   min-height/min-width hold the 48 dp Android touch floor even when a caller
   overrides font-size or padding inline. */
.cw-btn {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px;
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    min-height: 116px; min-width: 116px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);   /* clear the default runtime-Button grey */
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/ButtonGrayscale.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(171, 111, 57);
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 26px; padding-left: 44px; padding-right: 44px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.10s;
}
.cw-btn:hover  { scale: 1.03 1.03; }
.cw-btn:active { scale: 0.97 0.97; }
/* ONE BUTTON-COLOUR RULE (spec "Visual system"):
     green   the single forward action on a screen - PLAY SOLO, GEAR UP, READY,
             START MATCH. Tint is the CTA ramp #7be35c -> #36a82c divided by the
             atom's ~0.81 grey face so the bevel lands on the ramp.
     wood    navigation and secondary actions (HOME/BACK, gear, HOST/JOIN,
             ability lab, share/copy). #8a5a2e pushed the same way.
     gold    selection / "you" only - never a button.
   Labels are cream with the display ink outline on every face, which is what
   keeps them above 4.5:1 regardless of the face colour. */
.cw-btn--green   { -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(118, 238, 88); }
.cw-btn--wood, .cw-btn--neutral { -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(171, 111, 57); }
/* A disabled primary must still read as text, not as a ghost - 40% opacity on
   cream over the face drops under 4.5:1. Dim the face, keep the outlined label. */
.cw-btn:disabled { opacity: 1; -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(118, 98, 76); color: rgb(236, 226, 206); }

/* Focus ring — D-pad/keyboard navigation must have a visible indicator that
   is not color alone (same accessibility rule as every selected/picked state
   in this file). A bright border that appears only on focus is additive: none
   of these classes show a border normally (.cw-btn's is baked into its atom,
   0-width by default; the new Step 1/2 controls are borderless or tan by
   default), so this never fights their resting look. Added alongside the new
   Step 1/2 controls (.cw-slot-box, .cw-spec-pill) that introduced this file's
   first Buttons the player can reach by D-pad without a mouse hovering them
   first; extended to the shared .cw-btn/.cw-home-btn atoms too since they had
   no focus indicator at all before this pass. */
.cw-btn:focus, .cw-home-btn:focus, .cw-slot-box:focus, .cw-spec-pill:focus {
    border-left-width: 5px; border-right-width: 5px; border-top-width: 5px; border-bottom-width: 5px;
    border-left-color: rgb(254, 245, 224); border-right-color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    border-top-color: rgb(254, 245, 224); border-bottom-color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
}

/* Home/back button — absolutely placed at a header's top-left, leaves the
   centered ribbon undisturbed. */
.cw-home-btn {
    position: absolute; left: 28px; top: 28px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    min-height: 116px; min-width: 200px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/ButtonGrayscale.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(171, 111, 57);
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 22px; padding-left: 26px; padding-right: 26px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.1s;
}
.cw-home-btn:hover  { scale: 1.04 1.04; }
.cw-home-btn:active { scale: 0.96 0.96; }
/* Gear (settings) - same wood atom, mirrored to the top-right, square, and the
   glyph comes from Noto Emoji (.cw-glyph). Accessible name = its tooltip,
   resolved from settings.title by UiText.ResolveTree. */
.cw-gear-btn {
    left: auto; right: 28px;
    min-width: 116px; width: 116px; height: 116px;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 6px;
    font-size: 60px;
    -unity-text-outline-width: 0;
    /* Re-stated here: .cw-home-btn (later in this file than .cw-glyph) sets Lilita,
       which has no gear, and the OS colour-emoji fallback would draw it instead. */
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf");
}

/* ---- Ribbon --------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* The Stage-0 Ribbon atom is a grayscale banner-with-tails (9-slice 92,32),
   tinted gold at runtime — replaces the flat gold bar + Gloss sheen. The 92px
   side borders are the fixed tails, so content padding clears them. */
/* Painted-wood ribbon (spec: wood for frames and ribbons; gold is selection
   only). Tint = wood #8a5a2e pushed for the ~0.78 grey face. Title is cream
   with the display outline, not ink-on-gold any more. */
.cw-ribbon {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/Ribbon.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(178, 116, 60);
    padding-top: 14px; padding-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 96px; padding-right: 96px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
.cw-ribbon .cw-title { color: rgb(254, 245, 224); font-size: 52px; letter-spacing: 3px; -unity-text-outline-width: 5px; text-shadow: 0px 5px 0px rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.85); }

/* ============================================================================
   MAIN MENU  (2026-07-24 redesign — see Assets/UI/MainMenu.uxml for the why)
   Vertical budget on the 1080 canvas, distributed by the flex spacers in the
   page rather than by fixed offsets, so the block stays centred on any aspect:
       title block   ~230   cast band ~300   actions ~330   build stamp ~40
   ============================================================================ */
/* Painted farmyard-arena plate (Flux, 1344x768) behind the whole menu.
   scale-and-crop, NOT stretch-to-fill: the plate is 16:9 and the canvas is
   16:9, but a phone's safe area is not, and stretching a painted background
   is instantly visible where the fence lines skew. */
/* The plate itself moved to the shared backdrop (.cw-backdrop) in stage 2, and
   the flat dark scrim that used to knock it back was replaced by the per-page
   warm lift (.cw-backdrop-tint): legibility now comes from the display outline
   on every word that sits on the art, not from darkening the art. */
.cw-menu { align-items: center; justify-content: center; }

.cw-menu-titleblock { align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-menu-title    { font-size: 128px; letter-spacing: 8px; }
/* Lighter than the .cw-body tan: that tone was chosen against the flat #0e0804
   screen, and the glow lifts the backdrop enough here to erode its contrast. */
.cw-menu-subtitle {
    font-size: 34px; letter-spacing: 4px; margin-top: 6px;
}

/* ---- Cast band ------------------------------------------------------------
   The four playable chickens, which are the actual product. Sprites are the
   same Stage-0 exports the character select uses, so this costs no new art. */
.cw-menu-cast {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 44px; margin-bottom: 48px;
}
.cw-menu-cast__item { align-items: center; margin-left: 26px; margin-right: 26px; }
.cw-menu-cast__art  { width: 200px; height: 200px; }
.cw-menu-cast__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 10px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: nowrap;
}
/* The *light* class variants (--cw-class-*-light in CluckWarsTokens.uss), not the
   base tints. The base tints are tuned to sit on the flat #0e0804 screen; over the
   painted plate they land on dark green grass, where Warrior red (#C04030) and
   Assassin purple (#7B68EE) both fall below a readable ratio. Same hues, lifted. */
.cw-menu-cast__name--warrior  { color: rgb(240, 152, 136); }
.cw-menu-cast__name--speedy   { color: rgb(255, 176, 136); }
.cw-menu-cast__name--fatty    { color: rgb(255, 243, 176); }
.cw-menu-cast__name--assassin { color: rgb(196, 184, 255); }

/* ---- Actions --------------------------------------------------------------
   One primary, two secondary. Three identical pills gave the eye no entry
   point; SOLO is the instant-play path a playtester takes almost every time. */
.cw-menu-actions { align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-menu-primary {
    min-width: 620px; min-height: 148px;
    font-size: 58px; letter-spacing: 4px;
}
.cw-menu-secondary-row { flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; margin-top: 20px; }
.cw-menu-secondary {
    min-width: 300px;
    font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: 2px;
    margin-left: 12px; margin-right: 12px;
}
.cw-menu-hint {
    font-size: 32px; margin-top: 26px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* Build stamp. Bottom-left, deliberately quiet — it exists so a tester can say
   which build a bug came from, not to be read during play. */
.cw-menu-build {
    position: absolute; left: 28px; bottom: 20px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: rgba(254, 245, 224, 0.7);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 1px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}

/* ---- Class chip (Step 1 "Choose Your Chicken" card) ----------------------- */
/* One of only four, and the primary decision in the flow — 2026-09 split grew
   this from a flat 142px list row into a column card: it now also carries the
   pre-filled-slot tag and both specialization pills (one-tap class+spec select,
   Maestro's requirement), so it needs the vertical room. .cw-class-chip is
   scoped to Assets/UI/CharacterSelectClass.uxml only as of this split — the old
   Step-2 ClassList that shared this class is gone (see CharacterSelect.uxml) —
   so resizing it here does not touch the loadout screen. */
/* Direction A: a raised cream card with an ink outline. The selected chip's
   border (class tint) and faint class wash are set in C#
   (MenuUiController.RefreshClassSelect); its CardGlowFrame overlay is the
   .cw-glow child, shown by .cw-card--selected (see the value-steps block). */
.cw-class-chip {
    flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch;
    min-height: 210px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 16px; border-top-right-radius: 16px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 16px; border-bottom-right-radius: 16px;
    padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.cw-class-chip:hover { scale: 1.01 1.01; }
.cw-class-chip.cw-card--selected {
    border-left-width: 6px; border-right-width: 6px; border-top-width: 6px; border-bottom-width: 6px;
}
/* Landscape layout of the 4 cards is a 2x2 grid — see the .cw-cs-classes rules
   in the Responsive block at the bottom of this file for the width/height
   budget. Card height is content-driven (every label below is flex-shrink:0 and
   padding/margin-zeroed so its box equals its measured text), and the grid's
   align-content:stretch hands any leftover column height to the two rows. */
.cw-class-chip__toprow { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-class-chip__art { width: 76px; height: 76px; -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 14px; }
/* Name/role column. flex-shrink:0 so it can never be squeezed below its own
   text (it used to collapse to ~4px and paint WARRIOR over the tag); the
   pre-filled tag beside it is the element that yields instead. */
.cw-class-chip__titles { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-class-chip__name { font-size: 36px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); -unity-text-outline-width: 0; text-shadow: 0px 0px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); white-space: nowrap; -unity-text-align: middle-left; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; flex-shrink: 0; }
/* Role tag: soft brown on cream, ~7:1 (was tan #c4a060 on dark brown). */
.cw-class-chip__role { font-size: 28px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42); -unity-text-outline-width: 0; text-shadow: 0px 0px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); white-space: nowrap; -unity-text-align: middle-left; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-slot-pill {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px;
    padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 6px; padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px;
    border-top-left-radius: 12px; border-top-right-radius: 12px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    color: rgb(196, 160, 96);
}

/* Pre-filled-slot badge. The UXML text is only a placeholder — the controller
   overwrites it with "One slot pre-filled: <Ability>" (MenuUiController.
   RefreshPreFilledTags), ~310-360px at this size depending on the ability.
   Omitted on Assassin per Peck.asset's AllowedClasses. It is the flexible item
   in the top row: flex-shrink:1 + min-width:0 + white-space:normal let it wrap
   to a second line when a long ability name meets a narrow card, instead of
   squeezing the name/role column (.cw-class-chip__titles) to nothing. */
.cw-prefilled-tag {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; margin-left: 12px;
    padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 6px; padding-left: 14px; padding-right: 14px;
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
    /* Ink pill, cream text: ~15:1 on any card tint (was gold at 16% over a
       dark card, which measured under 3:1). */
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: normal;
}

/* ---- Specialization pills (Step 1) -----------------------------------------
   SpecOptA/SpecOptB. Directly tappable — Maestro's explicit requirement was
   one tap selects class AND specialization together, never a two-step
   "select the card, then pick a passive" flow (see
   MenuUiController.BindSpecPill/SelectClassAndPassive). Effect text is shown
   ALWAYS, not revealed only after selection — that visibility is the entire
   point of moving specializations onto the card instead of a name-only pill
   the old PassiveOptionRow used. min-height matches the 48dp touch floor like
   every other tappable control in this file, because this is a Button, not
   decoration. */
.cw-spec-pill-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; flex-grow: 1; }
.cw-spec-pill {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0;
    min-height: 116px;
    /* Top-aligned, stretched children: with justify-content:center, any text
       taller than the pill spilled out above AND below it (the name label sat
       at y=-15 over the top row). Stretch gives every label the full content
       width so its measured wrap height is deterministic. */
    align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);   /* inset cream well */
    background-image: none;                 /* Button atoms default to ButtonGrayscale — this is a card, not a pill button */
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35);
    border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.35);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px; padding-left: 12px; padding-right: 12px;
    margin-right: 5px; margin-left: 5px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.1s;
}
/* Every text child of a pill: never flex-shrunk below its text (the default
   flex-shrink:1 laid the desc out 7px tall and let it overflow onto the
   signature), and Unity's default Label margin/padding (~13px per label) zeroed
   so the pill's height budget is exactly the text. Text alignment is set
   explicitly because Button's default middle-center would otherwise inherit. */
.cw-spec-pill__name, .cw-spec-pill__desc, .cw-spec-pill__signature {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
    -unity-text-align: upper-left;
}
.cw-spec-pill:hover { scale: 1.02 1.02; }
.cw-spec-pill:active { scale: 0.98 0.98; }
/* Selected state must not be color-only (deuteranope guard, same rule as
   .cw-ability-card--picked below): scale + a widened border together, not a
   bare color swap. */
/* Gold = selection. Solid gold fill + ink border, ink text on it (~11:1);
   the old 18%-gold wash left the gold signature text at ~2:1. */
.cw-spec-pill--selected {
    scale: 1.03 1.03;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-spec-pill--selected .cw-spec-pill__desc,
.cw-spec-pill--selected .cw-spec-pill__signature { color: rgb(42, 26, 12); }
.cw-spec-pill__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap;
}
/* The effect line — 30px, the caption floor, not the 34px reading floor: two
   pills side by side in a half-width (2x2 grid) card leave ~290px of text
   width each at the 1920x1080 reference (~340px on a Pixel 9), i.e. 2-3 lines,
   and this text is genuinely informative (it is the whole reason the brief
   asked for "more info in the card"), so it gets the bigger of the two
   secondary sizes this file uses elsewhere (.cw-pick-row__hint,
   .cw-stat-label) rather than the 24-26px tertiary size .cw-cat-tag/.cw-cd-badge use. */
.cw-spec-pill__desc {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(74, 48, 24);
    white-space: normal; margin-top: 2px;
}
.cw-spec-pill__signature {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: rgb(122, 74, 34);
    white-space: normal; margin-top: 2px;
}

/* ---- Strong/weak role callouts (Step 1 preview panel) ---------------------
   Replaces the old numeric CARGO/RATE/SPEED stat-pip grid — Maestro rejected
   showing a fake numeric stat since nothing like it survived the GDD §2 combat
   rewrite (see MenuUiController.RefreshRoleCallouts). The label text itself
   ("STRONG: …" / "WEAK: …") is computed and written by the controller; the
   "+"/"−" glyphs beside each line are static siblings the controller never
   touches, so the strong/weak read never depends on color alone even though
   the controller doesn't split its own string into a separate colored prefix. */
.cw-role-list { width: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }
.cw-role-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.cw-role-glyph {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; width: 40px; flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center; margin-right: 8px;
}
.cw-role-glyph--pos { color: rgb(124, 217, 154); }
.cw-role-glyph--neg { color: rgb(232, 118, 108); }
.cw-role-callout {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; white-space: normal; flex-shrink: 1; flex-grow: 1; min-width: 0;
}
.cw-role-callout--strong { color: rgb(124, 217, 154); }
.cw-role-callout--weak   { color: rgb(232, 118, 108); }

/* ---- Chicken preview ------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Class figures are the Stage-0 design-exported sprites (Assets/_Game/Art/UI/
   Chickens/), applied by adding a .cw-chicken--<class> modifier in C#. These
   replaced the procedural UiGfx.Chicken() blobs in the Stage-3 fidelity pass.
   The base class only sets scale-mode so the same modifier paints the preview,
   the class-list chips, and the lobby player cards at their own sizes. */
.cw-chicken { -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit; }
.cw-chicken--warrior  { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Chicken_warrior.png"); }
.cw-chicken--speedy   { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Chicken_speedy.png"); }
.cw-chicken--fatty    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Chicken_fatty.png"); }
.cw-chicken--assassin { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Chickens/Chicken_assassin.png"); }
.cw-radial-glow {
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/RadialGlow.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    position: absolute;
}
/* Glowing circular platform behind the preview chicken (design §ColumnB).
   border-color + the inner radial glow tint are set in C# to the class color. */
.cw-preview-disc {
    width: 260px; height: 260px;
    border-top-left-radius: 130px; border-top-right-radius: 130px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 130px; border-bottom-right-radius: 130px;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgba(192, 64, 48, 0.5); border-right-color: rgba(192, 64, 48, 0.5);
    border-top-color: rgba(192, 64, 48, 0.5); border-bottom-color: rgba(192, 64, 48, 0.5);
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    overflow: visible;
}

/* ---- Stat bars (2-column grid, small pips — design §ColumnB) -------------- */
.cw-stat-grid { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; }
.cw-stat-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 10px; width: 48%; }
.cw-stat-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(196, 160, 96); width: 128px; margin-right: 10px;
}
.cw-stat-pips { flex-direction: row; }
.cw-pip {
    width: 16px; height: 26px; margin-right: 5px;
    border-top-left-radius: 3px; border-top-right-radius: 3px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 3px; border-bottom-right-radius: 3px;
    background-color: rgba(254, 245, 224, 0.2);   /* unfilled track — must stay visible */
}
.cw-pip--on { background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66); }

/* ---- Hex ability slot ----------------------------------------------------- */
/* The hex is the shared Stage-0 HexGlossy atom, tinted per-ability AccentColor
   in C# (empty slots get a dim neutral tint) — same sprite the touch HUD uses.
   Kept for the lobby / summary strips; the character-select picker no longer
   uses a slot-hex row (see the pick-row block below). */
.cw-hex {
    width: 116px; height: 134px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/HexGlossy.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
.cw-hex--active { scale: 1.08 1.08; }
/* "+" placeholder glyph, shown only while the slot is empty. */
.cw-hex__icon { font-size: 52px; -unity-text-align: middle-center; }
/* Exported ability icon sprite, shown once a slot is filled (icon painted by a
   .cw-hex-icon--* modifier). Sits on top of the tinted hex. */
.cw-hex__sprite {
    position: absolute;
    width: 68px; height: 68px;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
.cw-slot-caption {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(196, 160, 96); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* ---- Loadout slot boxes (Step 2, 2026-09 rework) ---------------------------
   #SlotBox0-3, one per active-ability slot — v0.7 made this uniform (4 slots
   for every class; COMBO no longer grants Assassin a 3rd). Replaces the old
   .cw-hex slot row: same job (show what is equipped and which slot the next
   tap acts on) but square, in a plain left-to-right row, and — unlike the hex,
   which only ever showed empty/filled — carrying a third ARMED state for the
   slot-arming machine (MenuUiController._armedSlot).

   Deliberately EMPTY of any base look here beyond size/shape: border color and
   background color for both the empty and filled states are set directly in
   C# (RefreshSlotBoxes -> SetBorder/style.backgroundColor), same pattern
   .cw-ability-card already uses for its picked state, so this class only needs
   to zero out the runtime Button's default chrome and hold the shape/spacing. */
.cw-slot-box-row { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 16px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-slot-box {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0;
    min-height: 180px;                        /* comfortably over the 116px/48dp floor; room for the STARTER tag */
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);       /* clear the default runtime-Button grey, see .cw-btn */
    background-image: none;
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
    margin-left: 6px; margin-right: 6px;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px; padding-left: 6px; padding-right: 6px;
    transition-property: scale, border-left-width, border-right-width, border-top-width, border-bottom-width;
    transition-duration: 0.12s;
}
/* Empty is dimmed, not just differently bordered — a slot with nothing in it
   should read as visually quieter than one that is filled, on top of the
   "EMPTY" label RefreshSlotBoxes adds as the non-color-only cue. */
/* No opacity any more: dimming the whole box also dimmed the EMPTY label under
   4.5:1. Empty reads quieter through the inset fill (set in C#) instead. */
.cw-slot-box__empty-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
}
/* Locked pre-equip tag: padlock glyph + STARTER, ink pill, >= 26 px (was an
   inline 9 px label). */
.cw-starter-tag {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 4px;
    padding-top: 2px; padding-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 12px; padding-right: 14px;
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
}
.cw-starter-tag__lock { font-size: 26px; color: rgb(245, 200, 66); margin-right: 6px; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; }
.cw-starter-tag__text {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
}
/* Armed = the slot the next ability-card tap will act on. A border-width bump
   plus a scale bump, not a color swap alone — this box's border color is
   already whatever SetBorder set it to (accent or neutral tan), so ARMED has
   to read through shape/size, exactly like .cw-ability-card--picked's scale
   bump reads through shape rather than relying on its own accent border. */
.cw-slot-box--armed {
    scale: 1.05 1.05;
    border-left-width: 6px; border-right-width: 6px; border-top-width: 6px; border-bottom-width: 6px;
}

/* ============================================================================
   LOADOUT PICK ROWS  (replaced the scrolling categorized ability grid)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ADR 0003 cut the pool a chicken can actually see to 3 Common + 3 Character.
   The old UI was a ScrollView of 23%-wide cards grouped under category headers
   — built when all 14 abilities were listed at once. With 3 items it rendered
   as up to three headers holding ONE card each, ~70% of every row empty, and a
   scroll view that never scrolled. It also required a two-step interaction
   (tap a slot hex, then tap a card) to choose between three things.

   The replacement is two flat rows, always fully visible, no scrolling:

       COMMON  — any chicken can take these (pool of 3)
       CLASS   — legal only for the selected class (pool of 3)

   Design override of GDD §7.1-7.2 (2026-07-27, reaffirmed by the user):
   Common is OPTIONAL, not a reserved 1st slot. The rows are a discoverability
   grouping only — tapping a card in EITHER row fills the next open slot among
   the N total active-ability slots (2 normally, 3 under Assassin's COMBO),
   freely mixed, no per-category minimum. Category survives as a colored tag
   on each card, which is where 4 labels for 3 items belongs.
   ============================================================================ */
/* Scroll container for the two pick rows - the ONLY scroll container on the
   loadout screen (stage 2 removed the per-row horizontal ScrollViews; nesting
   a horizontal scroller in a vertical one fought over every drag on a phone).

   `min-height: 0` is the whole trick and must not be removed. A flex item's
   default `min-height: auto` is its CONTENT height, so without this the
   ScrollView refuses to shrink below the full height of both pick rows, never
   scrolls, and overflows its parent exactly as the unscrolled markup did - the
   bug looks completely unfixed while the ScrollView is plainly present in the
   hierarchy. This is the single most common UI Toolkit scrolling mistake.

   The rows now WRAP their cards (see .cw-pick-cards): inside a vertical
   ScrollView a wrapped row simply makes the content taller, so the old
   "wrapped row paints over whatever sits below" bug cannot recur - that bug
   only ever happened when the wrapping grid was NOT inside a scroller. */
.cw-pick-scroll { flex-grow: 1; min-height: 0; }
.cw-pick-scroll .unity-scroll-view__horizontal-scroller { display: none; }
.cw-pick-scroll .unity-scroll-view__content-viewport { overflow: hidden; }
/* Room for the (now 34 px) themed scroller so the right-hand card and the
   "N EQUIPPED" counter never sit under it. */
.cw-pick-scroll .unity-scroll-view__content-container { padding-right: 16px; }

/* ---- Themed scrollbar (wood track, gold thumb, no arrow buttons) -----------
   Thick enough to grab with a thumb (34 px = ~14 dp; the whole column also
   drag-scrolls, so the bar is the secondary affordance). */
.cw-scroll .unity-scroller--vertical { width: 34px; margin-left: 6px; }
.cw-scroll .unity-scroller__low-button,
.cw-scroll .unity-scroller__high-button { display: none; }
.cw-scroll .unity-scroller--vertical > .unity-scroller__slider { margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; flex-grow: 1; }
.cw-scroll .unity-base-slider__tracker {
    background-color: rgb(122, 74, 34);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 17px; border-top-right-radius: 17px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 17px; border-bottom-right-radius: 17px;
}
.cw-scroll .unity-base-slider__dragger {
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(217, 165, 33); border-right-color: rgb(217, 165, 33);
    border-top-color: rgb(217, 165, 33); border-bottom-color: rgb(217, 165, 33);
    border-top-left-radius: 17px; border-top-right-radius: 17px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 17px; border-bottom-right-radius: 17px;
}
.cw-scroll .unity-base-slider--vertical .unity-base-slider__dragger { left: 0; width: 34px; margin-left: 0; }
.cw-scroll .unity-base-slider__dragger-border { display: none; }

/* Each pick row is a dark wood well (CardBg 9-slice) - the "panel" value step
   the cream cards sit on. */
.cw-pick-row { margin-bottom: 18px; padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 6px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px; }
.cw-pick-row__head { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.cw-pick-row__title {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    white-space: nowrap; margin-right: 16px;
}
.cw-pick-row__hint {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(232, 206, 158); white-space: nowrap;
}
/* Fills the remaining width so the "n / m" counter can sit hard right. */
.cw-pick-row__rule { flex-grow: 1; height: 2px; background-color: rgba(245, 200, 66, 0.35); margin-left: 16px; margin-right: 16px; }
.cw-pick-row__count {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); white-space: nowrap;
}
/* Cards WRAP inside the row since stage 2; the single vertical .cw-pick-scroll
   around both rows is what keeps a tall pool from painting over anything (see
   that rule). justify-content: flex-start so a short pool does not spread its
   cards to the edges. */
.cw-pick-cards { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-start; }

/* Fixed width + flex-shrink: 0, not the old width:32% — a percentage width
   inside a ScrollView's content container sizes against the SCROLLED content
   width (which has no fixed bound), not the visible viewport, so it no longer
   means anything useful once .cw-pick-cards stopped wrapping. This class is
   scoped to #CommonCards/#ClassCards only (MenuUiController.MakeAbilityCard is
   its only producer), so widening it here cannot affect anything else. */
.cw-ability-card {
    width: 290px; min-height: 160px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 16px; margin-bottom: 18px;
    align-items: center; justify-content: flex-start;
    padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 8px; padding-right: 8px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 16px; border-top-right-radius: 16px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 16px; border-bottom-right-radius: 16px;
    transition-property: scale; transition-duration: 0.1s;
}
.cw-ability-card:hover { scale: 1.04 1.04; }
/* Selection must not rely on the accent border alone — a red/green border swap
   is invisible to a deuteranope. The selected card also scales up and carries
   the numbered slot badge, so state is shape + position + color, never color
   on its own. */
.cw-ability-card--picked { scale: 1.04 1.04; }
.cw-ability-card__icon { font-size: 40px; height: 46px; -unity-text-align: middle-center; }
/* Exported ability icon sprite variant (Stage-3) — replaces the emoji glyph on
   the pick-row cards. Painted by a .cw-hex-icon--* modifier. */
/* flex-shrink:0 is load-bearing, not tidiness. This is a flex column, and a
   plain `height` is only a hint — when the card's children overflow, flexbox
   shrinks the shrinkable ones. The sprite has no text to floor it, so it
   collapsed to h=0 and the ability icons silently vanished from every pick
   card the moment per-card descriptions were added. Measured, not theorised:
   the per-card child dump read `cw-ability-card__sprite h=0.0` on all six.
   Descriptions now live in #AbilityDetail, so the icon is back at full size —
   but keep flex-shrink:0 so the next thing added to a card fails loudly
   (overflow) instead of silently eating the artwork. */
.cw-ability-card__sprite {
    width: 60px; height: 60px; flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
.cw-ability-card__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: nowrap; margin-top: 4px; margin-bottom: 4px;
}
/* Fallback when an ability has no authored sprite: its ShortLabel on its own
   accent disc (MenuUiController.MakeAbilityIcon). Always legible - text colour
   is picked against the accent (InkOn). Replaces the old emoji path, which
   rendered nothing when the class had no rule and the glyph was missing. */
.cw-ability-mono {
    width: 60px; height: 60px; flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 21px; letter-spacing: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 30px; border-top-right-radius: 30px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 30px; border-bottom-right-radius: 30px;
}
/* On a lobby mini-hex the hex itself is the accent disc; only the text shows. */
.cw-mini-hex .cw-ability-mono {
    width: auto; height: auto;
    font-size: 24px;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
}
/* One-line effect text (AbilityBaseSO.Description). flex-grow keeps the cooldown
   badge on the card's bottom edge, so badges stay aligned across a row whose
   cards carry one, two or three lines of copy. */
/* Category + cooldown side by side in one row rather than two stacked full-width
   rows. At ~43px each, stacking cost 86px of a 263px card. */
.cw-card-footer {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
.cw-card-footer .cw-cat-tag { margin-bottom: 0; margin-right: 8px; }

/* ---- Shared ability detail strip ------------------------------------------
   Descriptions were briefly rendered per-card at 24px (10.2 sp), which broke
   the contract at the top of this file AND collapsed the card icons to zero
   height. Six cards do not each need their own copy: only the ability the
   player just tapped is being considered. One strip means one description at
   the full 34px reading size, and it costs ~110px instead of ~275px (the two
   rows' worth of per-card description boxes it replaces).
   Reveal is plain tap — not long-press, which has no touch affordance. */
.cw-ability-detail {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center;
    min-height: 96px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 12px; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
}
.cw-ability-detail__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 16px;
}
.cw-ability-detail__text {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: normal; flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1;
}
/* Category tag — the taxonomy the old grid spent a full header row on, moved
   onto the card where 4 labels over 3 items makes sense. Fill set in C#. */
.cw-cat-tag {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    padding-top: 3px; padding-bottom: 3px; padding-left: 12px; padding-right: 12px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.cw-cd-badge {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    padding-top: 3px; padding-bottom: 3px; padding-left: 12px; padding-right: 12px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
}
/* On cream: dark text on a pale wash, both >= 5:1. */
.cw-cd-badge--short { background-color: rgb(214, 240, 200); color: rgb(30, 96, 30); }
.cw-cd-badge--med   { background-color: rgb(250, 230, 160); color: rgb(110, 72, 0); }

/* Numbered slot badge on a picked ability card — tells the player which
   in-match button (1/2/3, matching the touch HUD hex badges) will fire it.
   The circle's fill is set in C# to the ability accent color. */
.cw-ability-badge {
    position: absolute; top: -14px; right: -12px;
    width: 46px; height: 46px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(26, 14, 4); border-right-color: rgb(26, 14, 4);
    border-top-color: rgb(26, 14, 4); border-bottom-color: rgb(26, 14, 4);
    border-top-left-radius: 24px; border-top-right-radius: 24px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 24px; border-bottom-right-radius: 24px;
}

/* ============================================================================
   SETTINGS SHEET  (main menu gear -> modal; MainMenu.uxml #SettingsSheet)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Replaced the two toggles that used to sit on the loadout screen (#OptionsRow),
   which cost the phone pick list ~230 px. Four rows, each a whole-row touch
   target (MenuUiController.BindSettingRow toggles on a tap anywhere in it):
   name + one-line description on the left, the checkbox on the right.

   The checked state is carried by the BOX FILL (cream -> gold) and the ink
   tick, not only by the glyph: the checkmark image comes from the default
   runtime theme, and if that ever fails to resolve a glyph-only design would
   render ON and OFF identically.
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-sheet-scrim {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-color: rgba(20, 10, 4, 0.62);
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
.cw-sheet {
    width: 1180px; max-width: 94%; max-height: 96%;
    padding-top: 28px; padding-bottom: 32px; padding-left: 40px; padding-right: 40px;
    align-items: stretch;
}
.cw-sheet__head {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0; margin-bottom: 20px; min-height: 116px;
}
.cw-sheet__close { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 0; left: auto; min-width: 180px; }
.cw-sheet__body { padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 22px; padding-right: 22px; flex-shrink: 1; }
.cw-setting-toggle-row {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center;
    min-height: 116px;                        /* 48 dp floor - the whole row is the target */
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom-width: 2px; border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.18);
}
.cw-setting-toggle-row--last { border-bottom-width: 0; }
.cw-setting-toggle-row__texts { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; margin-right: 24px; }
.cw-setting-toggle-row__name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap; margin-left: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}
.cw-setting-toggle-row__desc {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    white-space: normal; margin-left: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0;
}

.cw-opt-toggle {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
}
/* Vertical centering ONLY. A Toggle is a BaseField, i.e. flex-direction: row -
   the theme pairs `flex-grow: 1` with `flex-basis: 0` on the input, so
   overriding grow to 0 collapses the input to zero width. Leave grow/basis. */
.cw-opt-toggle .unity-toggle__input { align-items: center; }
.cw-opt-toggle .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    width: 72px; height: 72px;
    margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 14px; border-top-right-radius: 14px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 14px; border-bottom-right-radius: 14px;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}
.cw-opt-toggle:checked .unity-toggle__checkmark {
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);      /* gold = selected */
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}

/* ---- Inset well + text input --------------------------------------------- */
.cw-well {
    background-color: rgba(10, 6, 2, 0.4);
    border-left-width: 2px; border-right-width: 2px; border-top-width: 2px; border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4); border-right-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4);
    border-top-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4); border-bottom-color: rgba(138, 106, 58, 0.4);
    border-top-left-radius: 16px; border-top-right-radius: 16px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 16px; border-bottom-right-radius: 16px;
}
.cw-input {
    background-color: rgb(26, 14, 8);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-right-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-color: rgb(106, 74, 40); border-bottom-color: rgb(106, 74, 40);
    border-top-left-radius: 12px; border-top-right-radius: 12px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;
    min-height: 116px; font-size: 48px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
}

/* ============================================================================
   Match Lobby (landscape: settings rail + 2×2 player grid — design §LobbyL)
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-lobby-body { flex-grow: 1; flex-direction: row; }

.cw-lobby-rail {
    width: 640px; flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px;
}
/* Rail cards are raised cream (.cw-raised) with ink text since stage 2. */
.cw-lobby-card {
    padding-top: 16px; padding-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px;
    margin-top: 14px;
}
.cw-lobby-cardlabel {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
}
.cw-lobby-cardhead {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 36px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); margin-bottom: 8px;
}

/* Gold invite-code letter tiles */
.cw-code-tiles { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 12px; }
.cw-code-tile {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 52px; color: rgb(26, 14, 4);
    background-color: rgb(212, 160, 32);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/GlossOverlay.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    border-left-width: 2px; border-right-width: 2px; border-top-width: 2px; border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgb(184, 138, 20); border-right-color: rgb(184, 138, 20);
    border-top-color: rgb(184, 138, 20); border-bottom-color: rgb(184, 138, 20);
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
    padding-top: 4px; padding-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
    margin-right: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px;
}

.cw-lobby-btnrow { flex-direction: row; margin-top: 14px; }
.cw-mini-btn {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0;
    min-height: 116px;
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/ButtonGrayscale.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: stretch-to-fill;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: rgb(171, 111, 57);   /* wood: secondary action */
    border-left-width: 0; border-right-width: 0; border-top-width: 0; border-bottom-width: 0;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
    margin-right: 12px;
}

/* Settings rows */
.cw-setting-row { flex-direction: row; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 8px; }
.cw-setting-k {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
}
.cw-setting-v {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}

/* Status pill */
/* Status line: cream inset, dark text (the status colour is set in C# from
   dark greens/browns that clear 4.5:1 on #f3e6c8). */
.cw-status-pill {
    flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 12px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 4px; border-right-width: 4px; border-top-width: 4px; border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
}
.cw-status-dot {
    width: 20px; height: 20px; margin-right: 14px;
    border-top-left-radius: 10px; border-top-right-radius: 10px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 10px; border-bottom-right-radius: 10px;
    background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66);
    border-left-width: 2px; border-right-width: 2px; border-top-width: 2px; border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-status-count {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 34px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); margin-right: 12px;
}
.cw-status-text {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); flex-grow: 1; -unity-text-align: middle-right;
}

.cw-lobby-start { letter-spacing: 2px; }
/* BACK is a wood navigation button (.cw-btn .cw-btn--wood) since stage 2; this
   class only spaces it under START. */
.cw-lobby-back { margin-top: 12px; }
.cw-lobby-error {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    margin-top: 10px; min-height: 38px; font-size: 32px;
    color: rgb(255, 150, 140); -unity-text-align: middle-center; white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-outline-width: 2px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}

/* Right column + player grid */
.cw-lobby-right {
    flex-grow: 1; min-width: 0;
    padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 20px; padding-left: 24px; padding-right: 24px;
}
.cw-players-head { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.cw-players-title {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); margin-right: 14px;
}
.cw-players-divider { flex-grow: 1; height: 4px; background-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.55); }

/* 2x2 grid. align-content is space-between in CSS terms, but Yoga in this
   Unity does not accept it for align-content (it logged a warning and fell
   back), so the rows are stretched and each card fills 48% of the height. */
.cw-player-grid {
    flex-grow: 1; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between; align-content: stretch;
}
/* Player card, stage-2 layout (fixes the 4:3 collisions):
     row 1   [art] [name ......(ellipsis)] [P-tag] [CPU/HOST]
                   [class . role (full width, ellipsis)]
     row 2   [ability hexes]                      [READY chip]   <- wraps
   The READY chip no longer shares a row with the class line, and the name
   gives way (ellipsis) instead of running into the P-tag. */
.cw-player-card {
    width: 49%; height: 48%; margin-bottom: 2%;
    flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; justify-content: center;
    padding-top: 14px; padding-bottom: 14px; padding-left: 26px; padding-right: 18px;
    background-color: rgb(255, 248, 232);
    border-left-width: 5px; border-right-width: 5px; border-top-width: 5px; border-bottom-width: 5px;
    /* border colour set in C# to the player colour */
    border-top-left-radius: 18px; border-top-right-radius: 18px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 18px; border-bottom-right-radius: 18px;
}
.cw-player-card--empty {
    background-color: rgba(243, 230, 200, 0.78);
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    border-left-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45); border-right-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45);
    border-top-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45); border-bottom-color: rgba(42, 26, 12, 0.45);
}
.cw-player-accent {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 12px;
    border-top-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-left-radius: 12px;
    /* color set in C# */
}
.cw-player-top { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
.cw-player-art {
    width: 120px; height: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 16px;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}
.cw-player-mid { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0; }
/* Wraps: on a narrow 4:3 card the P-tag / CPU tag drop under the name rather
   than the name being elided to "Da...". The name only ellipsises when it is
   wider than the whole column on its own. */
.cw-player-namerow { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; min-width: 0; }
.cw-player-name {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 40px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;
    flex-shrink: 0; max-width: 100%; margin-right: 14px;
    padding-left: 0; margin-left: 0;
}
/* P-tag: ink pill, cream text, a player-colour stripe on its left edge (set in
   C#). Player colours sit at ~3.9:1 against either cream or ink, so they mark
   the tag without carrying its text. */
.cw-player-pn {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 30px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224); flex-shrink: 0;
    background-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-left-width: 10px;
    padding-top: 2px; padding-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 12px;
    margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 2px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
}
/* HOST / CPU tag: cream inset with an ink border and ink text. */
.cw-player-host {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: rgb(42, 26, 12); flex-shrink: 0;
    background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200);
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 2px; padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 10px;
    border-top-left-radius: 8px; border-top-right-radius: 8px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 8px; border-bottom-right-radius: 8px;
}
.cw-player-host--host { background-color: rgb(245, 200, 66); }
.cw-player-class {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
    white-space: normal;                      /* full class line; wraps on 4:3 rather than eliding */
    margin-top: 4px; margin-left: 0; padding-left: 0;
}
.cw-player-bottom {
    flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
    margin-top: 12px; flex-shrink: 0;
}
.cw-player-chips { flex-direction: row; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 12px; }
.cw-mini-hex {
    width: 80px; height: 92px; margin-right: 6px;
    background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Atoms/HexGlossy.png");
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    align-items: center; justify-content: center;
}
/* Exported ability icon sprite on a lobby-card mini-hex. */
.cw-mini-hex__sprite {
    position: absolute;
    width: 54px; height: 54px;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

.cw-player-state {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 18px; padding-right: 18px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    border-top-left-radius: 12px; border-top-right-radius: 12px;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;
    border-left-width: 3px; border-right-width: 3px; border-top-width: 3px; border-bottom-width: 3px;
    border-left-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-right-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
    border-top-color: rgb(42, 26, 12); border-bottom-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-player-state--ready   { background-color: rgb(70, 170, 52); }
.cw-player-state--picking { background-color: rgb(243, 230, 200); }
.cw-player-state__label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/LilitaOne-Regular.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: rgb(254, 245, 224);
    -unity-text-outline-width: 3px; -unity-text-outline-color: rgb(42, 26, 12);
}
.cw-player-state--picking .cw-player-state__label { color: rgb(42, 26, 12); -unity-text-outline-width: 0; }
.cw-player-empty-label {
    -unity-font-definition: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Resources/Fonts/Nunito-Bold.ttf");
    font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: rgb(107, 74, 42);
}

/* ============================================================================
   Responsive — root carries .layout--portrait or .layout--landscape
   (toggled in C# from GeometryChangedEvent). Android is landscape-locked, so
   .layout--portrait only ever fires for a tall desktop/editor window.
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-cs-body { flex-grow: 1; }
.layout--portrait  .cw-cs-body { flex-direction: column; }
.layout--landscape .cw-cs-body { flex-direction: row; }

.layout--portrait  .cw-cs-classes { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; }
.layout--portrait  .cw-cs-classes .cw-class-chip { width: 49%; }
/* .cw-cs-body/.cw-cs-classes/.cw-cs-preview were the v3 design's 3-column
   single-screen layout (class list + preview fixed-width, loadout fills the
   rest). The 2026-09 class/loadout split retired the 3rd column: these three
   classes now belong to Step 1 (Assets/UI/CharacterSelectClass.uxml) only —
   classes + preview, 2 columns — while Step 2 (this file) uses `.cw-cs-detail`
   standalone below, with no `.cw-cs-body` row wrapping it at all, and gets the
   width the old loadout column never had (previously ~936px after the other
   two columns and page padding; now up to ~1872px, which is exactly why its
   pick-row cards could move from width:32%-and-wrap to a fixed 300px scroll —
   see .cw-ability-card in the LOADOUT PICK ROWS section). */
/* max-width 2240, not 1920: every 20:9 phone in the contract table lands on a
   ~2150x961 canvas (Pixel 9 2156x961), i.e. ~120px SHORTER than the 1080
   reference. A 1920 cap threw away the ~236px of extra width that the Step 1
   2x2 grid converts back into height (wider pills -> fewer desc lines); with
   the cap the bottom card row overflowed the Pixel 9 body by ~73px (measured).
   2240 still stops a 21:9 monitor (~2226 canvas) from stretching further. */
.layout--landscape .cw-cs-body { width: 100%; max-width: 2240px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
/* Step 1 class list, landscape: a 2x2 grid that takes ALL the body width the
   fixed preview column leaves (it used to be a 470px single column with ~950px
   of empty body to its right, and 4 stacked cards needing ~450px each against
   ~197px). Budget, measured with MeasureTextSize (desc 42px/line, signature
   34px/line, pill name 33px, card name+role 73px):
     width   1920 ref: body 1872 - preview 430 - margins 36 = 1406 -> card 49%
             = 689 -> pill text width ~290 -> desc <=3 lines, signature <=2
     height  card = border 6 + padding 20 + toprow 76 + 8 + pill (text <=241
             + padding 16 + border 6-8) ~= 365; 2 rows + 2x10 margin ~= 750
             <= 789 available in a 1920x1080 window.
     Pixel 9 canvas ~2156x961 -> list 1641 x 669 (needs the 2240 max-width on
             .cw-cs-body above): pill text width ~345 -> desc 2-3 lines,
             signature 1-2; natural rows ~295 + ~333 + 20 ~= 648 <= 669.
             That ~20px is the whole margin: a longer passive description
             that adds a desc line in the bottom row (+42) will overflow on
             phones. Re-run the ClassList layout probe after copy changes, and
             wrap #ClassList in a ScrollView if it ever stops fitting.
   Rows are content-sized; align-content:stretch gives any spare height to the
   two rows so the grid still fills the column. flex-grow/flex-basis:0 on the
   chips must NOT come back: basis 0 would let all 4 fit one wrap line. */
.layout--landscape .cw-cs-classes {
    flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between; align-content: stretch;
    flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; min-width: 0;
}
.layout--landscape .cw-cs-classes .cw-class-chip { width: 49%; flex-grow: 0; flex-shrink: 0; }

.layout--landscape .cw-cs-preview { width: 430px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-left: 18px; margin-right: 18px; }
.layout--portrait  .cw-cs-preview { width: 100%; margin-top: 14px; }

/* `min-height: 0` for the same reason as `.cw-pick-scroll`, one level up.
   Unlike .cw-cs-preview above, `.cw-cs-detail` is no longer ever a CROSS-axis
   item — since the split it is Step 2's ENTIRE body, with no `.cw-cs-body` row
   wrapping it in either orientation, so it is always a MAIN-axis (vertical)
   column item and `min-height: auto` would always resolve to content height.
   This line is what lets #PickScroll actually shrink to the space left after
   the slot-box row, AbilityDetail and READY, instead of
   overflowing onto them — not just a landscape/portrait guard the way it was
   before the split, when this column only ever hit the MAIN-axis case in the
   portrait mode the app doesn't ship. */
.cw-cs-detail { flex-grow: 1; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; }



.layout--portrait  .cw-mode-row { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
.layout--landscape .cw-mode-row { flex-direction: row; justify-content: center; }

/* Lobby reflow: landscape = rail + grid (default); portrait = stacked, 1-col cards */
.layout--portrait .cw-lobby-body { flex-direction: column; }
.layout--portrait .cw-lobby-rail { width: 100%; flex-shrink: 1; border-right-width: 0; }
.layout--portrait .cw-player-grid { flex-direction: column; flex-wrap: nowrap; }
.layout--portrait .cw-player-card { width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 18px; }

/* ============================================================================
   ABILITY ICON SPRITES  (14 : type-name -> exported Icon_*.png)
   Mirrors Assets/UI/Styles/TouchControls.uss so the character-select pick-row
   cards, slot hexes, and lobby mini-hexes paint the same Stage-0 design icons
   the touch HUD uses. The class applied to an element comes from the shared
   CluckWars.UI.AbilityIconStyle map (keyed by concrete ability SO type).
   These rules only set background-image — the element carries its own size via
   .cw-hex__sprite / .cw-ability-card__sprite / .cw-mini-hex__sprite.
   ============================================================================ */
.cw-hex-icon--dive-bomb {  background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_FlyingPeck.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--cluck    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_CluckShock.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--snatch    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_Peck.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--roll     { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_RollAndPush.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--trap     { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_FeatherTrap.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--aura     { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_FeatherAura.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--root     { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_RootEgg.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--shell    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_EggShell.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--turtle   { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_TurtleMode.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--spine    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_SpineCoat.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--burst    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_SpeedBurst.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--invis    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_Invisibility.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--doppel   { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_Doppelganger.png"); }
.cw-hex-icon--steal    { background-image: url("project://database/Assets/_Game/Art/UI/Icons/Icon_SneakySteal.png"); }
